  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Dover-Foxcroft is the county seat of Piscataquis County, Maine — the second-least-populous county east of the Mississippi River (after neighboring Aroostook). The town sits along the Piscataquis River at the outlet of Sebec Lake, in the central Maine interior between Bangor and the Moosehead Lake region.</p>
    <p>Despite the small population, Dover-Foxcroft has been a cannabis market since 2020 per the DabBars.org operator directory. The town's central location in the county — at the intersection of US Route 6 and Route 7 — makes it a natural access point for cannabis retail serving the surrounding Piscataquis County communities and the Moosehead Lake tourism corridor.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensary Operators in Dover-Foxcroft</h2>
    <p>Per the public directories (DabBars.org, Leafbuyer, and similar):</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dab Bar and Dispensary Dover-Foxcroft</strong> — operating since 2020. The operator's marketing notes that the Dover-Foxcroft team "are very knowledgeable about all of our marijuana and cannabis products" and that the operator "has been serving customers in Piscataquis County and surrounding areas since 2020."</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Use the Weedmaps Piscataquis County directory and the DabBars.org listing for the current full operator list, hours, and menus. The Piscataquis County market is small but stable.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Nearby Piscataquis County Markets</h2>
    <p><strong>Milo:</strong> GreenLife, an adult-use cannabis dispensary at 19 Park Street, opened in April 2023. Owned by Bob Ade, who was named the Piscataquis Chamber's [member of the year]. Milo is a small Piscataquis County town south of Dover-Foxcroft on US Route 11.</p>
    <p><strong>Greenville / Moosehead Lake:</strong> No dispensary cluster in Greenville itself. The Moosehead Lake tourism region draws visitors from across the Northeast, but cannabis access requires travel — to Dover-Foxcroft (60 min south), Bangor (90 min south), or the Somerset County / Skowhegan cluster to the west.</p>
    <p><strong>Sangerville / Guilford / Dexter:</strong> Small Piscataquis County towns along the Route 7 corridor. These communities rely on Dover-Foxcroft dispensaries. Dexter is at the southern edge of Piscataquis County and has its own small market.</p>
  </section>

